From 53c76813297ef19cb1ed9e25597d23c586eaab5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Kinder <nkinder@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Jan 2013 14:48:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Ticket 209 - TPS token enrollment causes DS syntax violations

This patch addresses a number of LDAP syntax violations that we
make in our common UG code as well as the TPS subsystem.  In all
of these cases, we are storing empty values for attributes that
use the "Directory String" syntax.  RFC 4517 states that a
"Directory String" value is 1 or more UTF8 characters.

The fix is to avoid storing empty attribute values for "Directory
String" attributes.  If we detect that we have an empty value, we
simply skip adding that attribute to the Directory Server.  We
also need to be careful that we don't have any code which can't
handle getting a NULL back when trying to retrieve an attribute
that may not exist in the DS instance.

With these changes, I am able to install and configure the CA, KRA,
TKS, and TPS subsystems and enroll a token using tpsclient without
any syntax errors from DS (with syntax checking enabled).
